  "slug": "automated-microscopy-2e31",
  "summary": "New spatial methods reassign transcripts, deconvolve spots and separate abundance from state, while OT frameworks reconstruct fate dynamics from snapshots.",
  "synthesis": "Two linked threads dominate. The first is attributing spatial measurements to cells and cell types. Tracel uses two-stage optimal transport to assign transcripts or bin counts to cells against matched scRNA-seq references. SSAF-T takes an agentic, segmentation-free route to cell-type inference and cell-type-guided segmentation. On the deconvolution side, spOT-NMF runs reference-free OT-NMF with proximity-aware niche mapping. SWIMR combines multiple reference panels with spatial correlation, and ARCADE separates cell-type abundance from continuous intratype state. SpatioCAD's density-aware graph diffusion reduces false-positive spatially variable genes, and OncoSpot simulates subclone- and CNA-aware data to benchmark tumor methods. The second thread is continuous dynamics from snapshots. LOTUS uses lineage-aware unbalanced OT, CytoBridge an unbalanced mean-field Schrödinger bridge on spatial data, and ManifoldVelo couples pseudotime with RNA velocity. BioTrajX scores the plausibility of inferred trajectories. GRN and perturbation work (REGA-perturb, CausalODE, GSET) is adjacent.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-07"
}
